<BaseLayout title="Checking engine oil level">
  <h1>Checking engine oil level</h1>
  <p>The 2021 S60 uses an electronic oil-level sensor. The displayed reading is only reliable when the vehicle has met the measurement conditions specified by Volvo.</p>

  <h2>Display the oil level</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Park the vehicle on a level surface.</li>
    <li>After driving, switch off the engine and allow the vehicle to remain stationary for at least 5 minutes.</li>
    <li>Open the Car Status app in the center display and select Status to view the oil-level graphic.</li>
    <li>If the display says the value is unavailable, do not treat that as a fault. Recheck after the required conditions have been met.</li>
  </ol>

  <div class="note"><strong>Volvo measurement condition:</strong> The owner's manual says the car may need to be driven approximately 30 km (20 miles), then left stationary for 5 minutes on a level surface with the engine off before the correct level is displayed.</div>

  <h2>Adding oil</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use only the specified oil grade for the engine code. For the 2021 T5 AWD engine alternatives listed by Volvo, this is Castrol Edge Professional V 0W-20 or VCC RBS0-2AE 0W-20.</li>
    <li>Do not use oil additives.</li>
    <li>Add oil gradually and recheck using the prescribed electronic measurement conditions. Do not overfill.</li>
    <li>If the oil-pressure warning appears, stop the vehicle as soon as safely possible and arrange towing/diagnosis. An oil-level reading does not rule out low oil pressure.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Important distinction</h2>
  <p>An oil-level warning and an oil-pressure warning are not interchangeable. Low oil pressure can indicate a serious lubrication problem even if the electronic oil-level display appears normal. Follow the exact driver-display instruction.</p>

  <h2>Source</h2>
  <p><a href="https://www.volvocars.com/us/support/car/s60/20w46">Volvo Cars — 2021 S60 owner's information</a>, “Checking and filling engine oil” and “Engine oil — specifications.”</p>
</BaseLayout>
